# =============================================================================
# provider box configuration — copy to .env and fill in.
# =============================================================================
# .env is gitignored. Five files are rendered from it by ./render.sh:
# provider.toml (A SECRET), connector.toml, operator-bearer.token,
# operator-write.keys and nginx/conf.d/node.conf.
#
# ── SINGLE-QUOTE ANYTHING WITH A SPACE OR A BRACE ────────────────────────────
# This file is read twice, by two parsers. docker compose reads it itself, and
# ./render.sh and ./bootstrap.sh `source` it as shell — where an unquoted value
# with a space runs its second word as a command, and an unquoted `{"a":"b"}`
# loses its quotes and stops being JSON. Single quotes satisfy both: compose
# strips them, and the shell takes the value whole.

# ── Required ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The zone this box's hostnames live under. Two A-records must point here:
#   proxy.provider.${DOMAIN}   the paid ILP edge
#   provider.${DOMAIN}         GET /health, and nothing else
DOMAIN=devnet.toonprotocol.dev

# This box's PUBLIC IPv4. It is where tenants reach their workloads — the
# daemon publishes each lease's SSH forward and its sixteen ports on it — and
# it is published in the Provider Profile. A container address here is a
# provider nobody can use.
PUBLIC_IP=

# What the Profile calls this provider. Free text, shown in a directory.
PROVIDER_NAME='TOON Devnet Provider'

# ── THIS PROVIDER'S IDENTITY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 64 hex characters:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# It signs the Profile, every Listing, every Liveness and every Eviction
# Notice, and it is the key a Lease Request is addressed to. It goes INLINE
# into the rendered provider.toml — which is why that file is 0600 and
# gitignored, unlike every other rendered config in this fleet.
#
# Changing it makes this a different provider: a new pubkey, an empty
# directory entry, and every tenant holding a lease addressed to the old one
# left talking to nobody. Record it somewhere off this box.
NOSTR_PRIVATE_KEY=

# ── The relay ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The relay READ url this provider publishes to and names in its Profile. A
# tenant reads the directory here; this provider also searches it for Blob
# Records by digest, which is how an image named by digest alone resolves.
RELAY_WS=wss://relay-ws.devnet.toonprotocol.dev

# The same relay's client edge, where its PAID write route is bought. The
# publisher opens a channel against this node and pays it per write.
RELAY_EDGE_URL=https://proxy.relay.devnet.toonprotocol.dev

# Relay READ url -> the PAID ILP destination that writes to it. JSON. Never a
# `.ephemeral` destination: the free lane's rate limit is keyed by remote
# address and shared by everyone behind one connector, and directory events
# are paid replaceable events (ADR 0007). The publisher refuses to start if
# this names one.
RELAY_WRITE_ROUTES='{"wss://relay-ws.devnet.toonprotocol.dev":"g.toon.relay"}'

# ── The wallet that pays for relay writes ────────────────────────────────────
# A BIP-39 phrase, and ITS OWN, shared with nothing: two payers on one channel
# share one nonce watermark, and the loser of that race has every later claim
# refused. It holds money and never identity — it cannot forge a directory
# event, only decline to pay for one.
#
# Fund the Solana address it derives with devnet SOL and mock USDC; see
# README.md § "The two funded identities".
PUBLISHER_MNEMONIC=''

# Where Let's Encrypt sends expiry warnings.
LETSENCRYPT_EMAIL=you@example.com

# Leave at 1 until DNS resolves to this box, then set 0 and re-run
# ./init-letsencrypt.sh. Staging certificates are untrusted by browsers but do
# not burn the production rate limit while you are still wiring DNS up.
LETSENCRYPT_STAGING=1

# ── The operator surface's two credentials ───────────────────────────────────

# Gates the connector's /metrics and redeem endpoints — which also means it is
# how this provider's earnings are redeemed, so it is not optional in practice.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
OPERATOR_BEARER_TOKEN=

# The ED25519 PUBLIC key permitted to sign operator writes — 64 hex
# characters, and NOT a nostr npub, a secp256k1 key or base58. Generate the
# private half OFF THIS BOX and keep it there:
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32 > operator-write.key    # keep this elsewhere
#   docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/d:ro" \
#     ghcr.io/toon-protocol/connector:rust-2026.09.11.1 \
#     send --operator-key /d/operator-write.key --print-keyid
#
# Revoke a key by changing this line, re-rendering and restarting.
OPERATOR_WRITE_KEY=

# ── Written by bootstrap.sh; do not fill in by hand ──────────────────────────

# This box's connector's own sealing key, copied verbatim from
# `GET /ilp/identity` INCLUDING the `0x`. A tenant compares it byte for byte
# against what the connector answers and refuses to spawn if they differ
# (ADR 0011), so it is a COPY OF A FACT and not a setting. bootstrap.sh starts
# the connector, reads it and appends it here, which is the only way to get it
# right without transcribing a 130-character hex string.
#
# Re-generate signer.key and you must delete this line and re-run bootstrap.sh.
# CONNECTOR_SEAL_KEY=

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The branch this box follows. `auto-apply.sh` fast-forwards it every five
# minutes and applies what it finds. It is a variable rather than a literal
# because the devnet provider runs ahead of this repository's `main` while a
# milestone is unmerged.
# TRACK_BRANCH=main

# The Solana RPC the publisher settles against.
# SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://api.devnet.solana.com

# An existing certificate lineage to keep using, if this box already has one
# filed under a different name. Defaults to proxy.provider.${DOMAIN}.
# CERT_NAME=
